#N canvas 0 0 500 550 10;
#X obj 10 20 inlet;
#X text 110 20 send a 3-float list: rate loopEndSamples loopStartSamples to update parameters atomically. send bang to retrigger from loop start.;
#X obj 10 60 route bang;
#X msg 10 100 0;
#X obj 150 100 unpack f f f;
#X obj 150 150 -;
#X obj 280 150 *;
#X obj 280 200 /;
#X obj 10 250 phasor~;
#X obj 10 300 *~;
#X obj 10 350 +~;
#X obj 10 400 tabread4~ \$1;
#X obj 10 450 outlet~;
#X text 150 450 known limitation: tabread4~'s 4-point interpolation window can read up to about 2 samples outside loopStart..loopEnd at the loop seam. no crossfade yet. creation arg: play_loop~ tableName (just the one -- see turn 9 note below for why sampleRate is no longer a creation arg).;
#X text 150 490 verified 2026-09-17 (turn 6) against a live Pd 0.56.5 install: loads clean via pd -nogui \, both the bang-retrigger and the set-parameters list process without error \, and the range/frequency arithmetic (unpack right-to-left firing order) was checked standalone against known inputs (rate 2 \, loopEnd 2000 \, loopStart 1000 -> range 1000 \, freq 88.2 at 44100sr) and matched. Not yet verified: actual audio output against a real sample \, since tabread4~ reads zeros from an untouched test array.;
#X text 150 530 turn 9 (2026-09-17) real-audio test found a real bug -- not in this abstraction \, in how it was being called: a test passed sampleRate=44100 as \$2 \, but this machine's actual Pd engine runs at 48000Hz ([samplerate~] confirms it). The loop played about 8% too slowly as a direct result -- position tracking was otherwise perfect (correlation 1.0 against a known ramp once the right rate was used). Rather than leave this as a footgun for the next caller \, sampleRate is no longer a creation argument at all: [loadbang] -> [samplerate~] queries the actual running engine rate once at load time and feeds it into the frequency multiply directly \, so it can never be wrong. Verified against a real loaded WAV (linear ramp \, tests/gen_test_wav.py + tests/test_play_loop_audio.pd): captured output vs. expected ramp \, correlation coefficient 1.000000 \, mean absolute error 0.003% of full-scale range \, perfectly monotonic across all 4409 steps.;
#X obj 10 570 loadbang;
#X obj 10 610 samplerate~;
